      "hints": [
        "Area under curve from $\\frac{1}{3}$ to $3$: $\\int_{1/3}^3 \\frac{1}{16}(3x - 1)^2 dx = \\frac{32}{9}$.",
        "Area of triangle under tangent: $\\frac{1}{2}(3 - \\frac{5}{3})(4) = \\frac{8}{3}$.",
        "Shaded area: $\\frac{32}{9} - \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{8}{9}$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Integrate under the curve from $P(1/3, 0)$ to $Q(3, 4)$:\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\text{curve}} = \\int_{1/3}^3 \\frac{1}{16}(3x - 1)^2\\,dx = \\left[ \\frac{(3x - 1)^3}{16 \\times 3 \\times 3} \\right]_{1/3}^3 = \\left[ \\frac{(3x - 1)^3}{144} \\right]_{1/3}^3$$",
        "Evaluate at the limits $x = 3$ and $x = \\frac{1}{3}$:\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\text{curve}} = \\frac{(3(3) - 1)^3}{144} - \\frac{(3(1/3) - 1)^3}{144} = \\frac{8^3}{144} - 0 = \\frac{512}{144} = \\frac{32}{9}$$",
        "Calculate the area of the right-angled triangle under the tangent line from $R(5/3, 0)$ to $x = 3$ (base $3 - \\frac{5}{3} = \\frac{4}{3}$, height $y_Q = 4$):\n$$\\text{Area}_{\\triangle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{4}{3} \\times 4 = \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{24}{9}$$",
        "Subtract the triangle area from the curve area to find the shaded area $PQR$:\n$$\\text{Shaded Area} = \\text{Area}_{\\text{curve}} - \\text{Area}_{\\triangle} = \\frac{32}{9} - \\frac{24}{9} = \\frac{8}{9}\\text{ square units} \\quad (\\approx 0.889)$$"
